questions.prompt:
Derive the following Maxwell's Demon, Information, and the Second Law relation from the preceding result, showing the algebra, calculus, counting, or thermodynamic identity used at each step.
\[
\Delta S_{\mathrm{env,min}}
=\frac{Q_{\mathrm{erase,min}}}{T_M}
=k_{\mathrm B}\ln2.
\tag*{[3]}
\]
Notation: \(k_{\mathrm B}\) denotes Boltzmann constant; unit \(\mathrm{J K^{-1}}\); \(T_M\) denotes absolute temperature of the memory's thermal environment; unit \(\mathrm{K}\); \(N\) denotes number of independent unbiased binary memory bits reset without usable side information; dimensionless; \(Q_{\mathrm{erase,min}}\) denotes minimum heat rejected during logically irreversible memory erasure; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(\Delta S_{\mathrm{env,min}}\) denotes minimum entropy increase of the erasure environment; unit \(\mathrm{J K^{-1}}\); \(\Delta S_{\mathrm{gas}}\) denotes entropy change of the sorted gas; unit \(\mathrm{J K^{-1}}\); \(\Delta S_{\mathrm{controller+memory+environment}}\) denotes combined entropy change of the controller, memory, and environment; unit \(\mathrm{J K^{-1}}\); \(\Delta S_{\mathrm{total}}\) denotes entropy change of gas, controller, memory, and environment; unit \(\mathrm{J K^{-1}}\); \(W_{\mathrm{mech}}\) denotes mechanical work done by the sorting gate; unit \(\mathrm{J}\).

Derive the following Maxwell's Demon, Information, and the Second Law relation from the preceding result, showing the algebra, calculus, counting, or thermodynamic identity used at each step.
\[
\Delta S_{\mathrm{total}}
=\Delta S_{\mathrm{gas}}
+\Delta S_{\mathrm{controller+memory+environment}}
\geq0.
\tag*{[5]}
\]
Notation: \(k_{\mathrm B}\) denotes Boltzmann constant; unit \(\mathrm{J K^{-1}}\); \(T_M\) denotes absolute temperature of the memory's thermal environment; unit \(\mathrm{K}\); \(N\) denotes number of independent unbiased binary memory bits reset without usable side information; dimensionless; \(Q_{\mathrm{erase,min}}\) denotes minimum heat rejected during logically irreversible memory erasure; unit \(\mathrm{J}\); \(\Delta S_{\mathrm{env,min}}\) denotes minimum entropy increase of the erasure environment; unit \(\mathrm{J K^{-1}}\); \(\Delta S_{\mathrm{gas}}\) denotes entropy change of the sorted gas; unit \(\mathrm{J K^{-1}}\); \(\Delta S_{\mathrm{controller+memory+environment}}\) denotes combined entropy change of the controller, memory, and environment; unit \(\mathrm{J K^{-1}}\); \(\Delta S_{\mathrm{total}}\) denotes entropy change of gas, controller, memory, and environment; unit \(\mathrm{J K^{-1}}\); \(W_{\mathrm{mech}}\) denotes mechanical work done by the sorting gate; unit \(\mathrm{J}\).

